# ==== T-FMT-B — TYPE-lexeme VERBATIM: the `byte` / `uint8` synonym pair, and
# the non-synonym primitives that must NOT move.
# SCOPE CLAIM: `Type::Primitive` spellings. `byte` is a user-facing alias the
# LEXER folds into `Keyword::Uint8` (`src/lexer/token.rs`), so the AST keeps no
# record of which spelling the author chose — exactly the radix situation, and
# it takes the same span-recovery cure.
# Pre-fix RED: `byte x` came back as `uint8 x` everywhere — in declarations,
# in parameter lists, in return types, in generic arguments, and in slices.
# Every position named there has a cell below; the generic-argument pair was
# added after an output-review measured that the header named a position the
# file did not sample (Core #12 — a fixture's NAME is a claim about SCOPE).
byte scale(byte v, uint8 already_canonical):
    return v + already_canonical

byte[] widen(byte[] xs):
    return xs

Vector[byte] buffer(Dict[String, byte] table):
    return []

void main():
    byte a = 1
    uint8 b = 2
    print(scale(a, b))
